{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>to make known to the children of man</b> — that they are small." "<b>and the vav of גבורותיו</b> — [regarding] \"they shall speak of the glory of Your kingdom\": there is no objection to how \"the glory of the majesty of His kingdom\" is joined to \"the glory of Your kingdom,\" for behold its like: \"until King of the kingdom of Persia\" [Daniel], and our early ones fixed in prayer: וימליך מלכותיה (\"and establish His kingdom\"). Likewise the verse: ומלכותו בכל משלה (\"and His kingdom rules over all\")."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 145, :notes {0 "The comment defines לבני האדם as implying human insignificance; no textual difficulty.", 1 "The phrase עד מלך מלכות פרס alludes to Daniel 6:29 (Aramaic); Ibn Ezra cites it in Hebrew. The prayer cited appears to be a variant of a known liturgical passage; resolved by inference to the standard formula."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:42:53.257465111Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}